#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""update-factory — refresh an installed .agent-factory/factory/ to the current checkout.

What: Brings a project's installed `.agent-factory/factory/` up to date with
      a candidate source (a local checkout or the recorded remote release),
      through the seven-step transaction from ADR-0023: check, approval,
      download-and-verify, staging, application, rollback, and receipt.
      Application re-applies every *derived* install step through the
      sourced init-factory — regenerated Codex adapters and Copilot agent
      copies (with tools: frontmatter), re-verified runtime symlinks,
      re-merged guardrail/usage hook wiring, and a re-run pre-commit
      install.
When: To update an existing install to a newer checkout or release.
By:   run by hand (a shell, no AI needed); companion to init-factory and
      remove-factory. Run it from the checkout (`--target <project>`) or from
      inside the installed project (`--source <checkout>`); either works.

Local-change safety: Before staging, the script compares per-file checksums
recorded at install time against the currently installed files. Files that
the user added (custom skills, agents, scripts) or modified (tweaked prompts,
adjusted rules) are detected and reported. When user changes are found, the
update stops unless --force is passed. With --force, user-changed and
user-added files are preserved in .agent-factory/user-changes/ so
nothing is lost.

Installations created before checksum recording was introduced have no
baseline to compare against. In that case the update proceeds as before
(full replacement) and records checksums for future updates.

Paths a pre-commit hook regenerates after install (see HOOK_REGENERATED_PATHS,
currently INDEX.yaml) are excluded from checksum comparison entirely: a hook
doing its job is never a user modification, so it never triggers --force.
These paths are still overwritten on every update, same as everything else in
.agent-factory/factory/ — they are just never diffed against the baseline.

Approval: once local changes clear, a preview shows the source, installed
and candidate versions, and planned effects (the factory/ replacement plus
any instruction-header additions or content changes). Blank, declined, or
cancelled input is never treated as consent — no download or mutation
happens before an explicit "yes".

Download and verification: for a remote-sourced install, the candidate
archive is downloaded and its SHA-256 digest verified against SHA256SUMS
before any extraction. A missing or mismatched digest aborts with no
changes. A local source is used as-is (there is no published digest for an
arbitrary checkout).

Staging: the verified candidate is copied into
`.agent-factory/factory-staging-<uuid>`, alongside the current installation.
Nothing under `.agent-factory/factory/` is touched during staging.

Application: the current `.agent-factory/factory/` is moved aside to
`.agent-factory/factory-backup-<uuid>` (not deleted), the staged replacement
is swapped into place, instruction-header edits are applied, and the sourced
init-factory re-derives per-CLI wiring against the new tree.

Rollback: if application fails — the swap, a header edit, or the sourced
init-factory returning non-zero — the previous `.agent-factory/factory/`,
`install.json` manifest, `checksums.json`, and any touched instruction
headers are restored exactly. The project is never left without a
`.agent-factory/factory/`; resolve the reported failure and re-run
`update-factory` to finish.

What is *not* touched: only `.agent-factory/factory/`, `install.json`,
`checksums.json`, and instruction-header content are written. The project's
own files, the `.gitignore`/`.pre-commit-config.yaml` edits, and the rest of
`.agent-factory/` — including the usage-tracking transcripts under
`.agent-factory/usage/` and the lifecycle state under `.agent-factory/usage/
control/` — are all preserved. init-factory never deletes usage data.

The one decision update-factory cannot infer is WHICH checkout or release to
pull from. init-factory records the source it copied from in the install
manifest (`factory_source` for local, `source_selector`/`resolved_source`
for remote); update-factory reads that as its default and `--source`
overrides it for a local candidate of the *same* source kind. Installations
created before that field existed must pass `--source`.

Source boundary: `--from-remote <URL>` or `--from-local <path>` request a
source kind change (local<->remote) or a different remote base URL — a
trust-boundary change (VFO-005, ST-0286). That requires its own separate
"yes", shown before the normal update approval; declining stops with no
changes, and `--force` never bypasses it. Same source kind and same URL is
not a boundary change — no separate prompt, just the normal approval.

Usage
  update-factory --target /path/to/project                 # source from manifest
  update-factory --target /path/to/project --source /path/to/agent_factory
  update-factory --source /path/to/agent_factory           # target = cwd
  update-factory --check                                   # report changes, don't update
  update-factory --force                                   # update despite user changes
  update-factory --from-remote https://other.example.com   # source-boundary change (remote URL)
  update-factory --from-local ./factory-src                # source-boundary change (to local)

--check reports installed and candidate versions, source, candidate digest,
local modifications, and planned instruction header changes, and performs no
writes: no files, directories, staging areas, or manifest updates. The
candidate version comes from the source's packages/factory/VERSION (local)
or from the same remote release resolution install-agent-factory uses
(remote, without downloading the archive). It always exits 0 once the
manifest is readable, whether or not changes are found — --check reports,
it never gates.

Exit code: 0 on success, including --check. 1 if the target isn't an
init-factory'd project, if no source can be resolved, if consent is
declined, if archive verification fails, or if application fails after
rollback. 2 if user modifications were detected on a non-check run and
--force was not passed.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tarfile
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

MANIFEST_PATH = ".agent-factory/install.json"
CHECKSUMS_PATH = ".agent-factory/checksums.json"
USER_CHANGES_DIR = ".agent-factory/user-changes"
CHECKSUM_SKIP_PREFIXES = ("__pycache__/",)
CHECKSUM_SKIP_SUFFIXES = (".pyc",)
REMOTE_TIMEOUT = 30

# ADR-0023 seven-step transaction: the staging and backup directories live
# alongside the current installation under .agent-factory/, never outside
# it, so the whole transaction stays in the project's factory-managed
# namespace.
STAGING_DIR_PREFIX = "factory-staging-"
BACKUP_DIR_PREFIX = "factory-backup-"
REMOTE_SCRATCH_PREFIX = "factory-remote-"

# Instruction-file discovery, mirroring install-agent-factory's rule, so
# --check can tell which files would receive a header on the next update
# without delegating to init-factory (which --check must never invoke).
INSTRUCTION_FILENAMES = frozenset({"AGENTS.md", "copilot-instructions.md"})
INSTRUCTION_SCAN_SKIP_DIRS = frozenset({
    ".git", "node_modules", "__pycache__", ".venv", "venv", ".tox", ".nox",
    "dist", "build", ".eggs", ".mypy_cache", ".pytest_cache", ".ruff_cache",
    "factory", ".agent-factory", ".current-work", ".claude", ".github", ".pi",
    ".codex", ".agents",
})

# Orientation block markers and per-CLI content sources, duplicated from
# install-agent-factory (kept in sync the same way HOOK_REGENERATED_PATHS
# is — see TestHookRegeneratedPathsConstant) so --check can recompute what
# header content a *local* candidate source would produce, for content-level
# comparison against the installed block_digest.
ORIENTATION_BEGIN = "<!-- >>> agent_factory orientation >>>"
ORIENTATION_END = "<!-- <<< agent_factory orientation <<< -->"
ORIENTATION_INCLUDE = {
    ".claude": "@../../.agent-factory/factory/config/AGENTS.claude.md\n@../docs/agent-context.md\n",
}
CLI_DOT_DIRS = {
    "claude": [".claude"],
    "copilot": [".github"],
    "pi": [".pi"],
    "codex": [".codex"],
}
CLI_ORIENTATION_FILE = {
    ".claude": "AGENTS.claude.md",
    ".github": "AGENTS.copilot.md",
    ".pi": "AGENTS.pi.md",
    ".codex": "AGENTS.codex.md",
}

# Paths (relative to factory/) that a pre-commit hook regenerates after
# install — e.g. index-lint rewriting INDEX.yaml. These are never a user
# choice, so they are excluded from checksum comparison here: a hook-
# modified file must never be reported as a "user modification" that
# requires --force. Kept in sync with the identical constant in
# init-factory; the full factory/ replace below still overwrites these
# paths unconditionally, since update-factory never copies file-by-file.
HOOK_REGENERATED_PATHS = ("INDEX.yaml",)


def _unlock_factory(factory_dir: Path) -> None:
    """chmod u+w on all files so the directory can be moved/deleted."""
    import stat
    for root, _dirs, files in os.walk(factory_dir):
        for name in files:
            p = Path(root) / name
            p.chmod(p.stat().st_mode | stat.S_IWUSR)


def _is_hook_regenerated(rel: str) -> bool:
    return any(rel == p or rel.endswith(f"/{p}") for p in HOOK_REGENERATED_PATHS)


def _lock_factory(factory_dir: Path) -> None:
    """chmod a-w on installed factory/ files when packages/factory/ exists."""
    if not (factory_dir.parent / "packages" / "factory").is_dir():
        return
    import stat
    for root, _dirs, files in os.walk(factory_dir):
        for name in files:
            p = Path(root) / name
            rel = p.relative_to(factory_dir).as_posix()
            if _is_hook_regenerated(rel):
                continue
            p.chmod(p.stat().st_mode & ~(stat.S_IWUSR | stat.S_IWGRP | stat.S_IWOTH))


class ManifestUnreadable(Exception):
    """The install manifest exists but cannot be read as valid JSON."""


def log(line: str) -> None:
    print(f"update-factory: {line}")


def load_manifest(target: Path) -> dict | None:
    """Return the install manifest, None if it is absent, or raise
    `ManifestUnreadable` if it exists but is malformed — so callers can
    distinguish "not an install" from "an install whose manifest is corrupt"."""
    path = target / MANIFEST_PATH
    if not path.exists():
        return None
    try:
        manifest = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError) as exc:
        raise ManifestUnreadable(str(exc)) from exc
    return manifest if isinstance(manifest, dict) else None


# ── Checksum detection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────


def _should_checksum(rel: str) -> bool:
    return (
        not any(rel.startswith(p) or f"/{p}" in rel for p in CHECKSUM_SKIP_PREFIXES)
        and not any(rel.endswith(s) for s in CHECKSUM_SKIP_SUFFIXES)
        and not any(
            rel == p or rel.endswith(f"/{p}") for p in HOOK_REGENERATED_PATHS
        )
    )


def _compute_checksums(factory_dir: Path) -> dict[str, str]:
    checksums: dict[str, str] = {}
    for path in sorted(factory_dir.rglob("*")):
        if not path.is_file():
            continue
        rel = path.relative_to(factory_dir).as_posix()
        if not _should_checksum(rel):
            continue
        checksums[rel] = hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
    return checksums


def _read_checksums(target: Path) -> dict[str, str] | None:
    path = target / CHECKSUMS_PATH
    if not path.exists():
        return None
    try:
        data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        files = data.get("files")
        return files if isinstance(files, dict) else None
    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):
        return None


def _write_checksums(target: Path, factory_dir: Path) -> None:
    checksums = _compute_checksums(factory_dir)
    out = target / CHECKSUMS_PATH
    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    out.write_text(
        json.dumps({"version": 1, "files": checksums}, indent=2) + "\n",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )


def _detect_modifications(
    target: Path,
) -> tuple[list[str], list[str], list[str]] | None:
    """Compare installed factory/ against stored checksums.

    Returns (modified, added, removed) lists of relative paths, or None
    when no baseline checksums exist (pre-checksum install).
    """
    stored = _read_checksums(target)
    if stored is None:
        return None

    factory_dir = target / ".agent-factory" / "factory"
    if not factory_dir.is_dir():
        return None

    current = _compute_checksums(factory_dir)

    modified = [r for r in current if r in stored and current[r] != stored[r]]
    added = [r for r in current if r not in stored]
    removed = [r for r in stored if r not in current]

    return modified, added, removed


def _report_modifications(
    modified: list[str], added: list[str], removed: list[str],
) -> None:
    """Print a human-readable report of user changes."""
    total = len(modified) + len(added) + len(removed)
    print(f"\n  Found {total} user change(s) in .agent-factory/factory/:\n")
    if modified:
        print("  Modified (content differs from install baseline):")
        for f in modified:
            print(f"    M  {f}")
    if added:
        print("  Added (not in original install):")
        for f in added:
            print(f"    A  {f}")
    if removed:
        print("  Removed (present at install, now absent):")
        for f in removed:
            print(f"    D  {f}")
    print()


def _preserve_user_changes(
    target: Path, modified: list[str], added: list[str],
) -> Path | None:
    """Copy user-modified and user-added files to a dated directory.

    Returns the directory path, or None if there was nothing to preserve.
    """
    to_save = modified + added
    if not to_save:
        return None

    from datetime import datetime

    stamp = datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
    dest = target / USER_CHANGES_DIR / stamp
    factory_dir = target / ".agent-factory" / "factory"

    for rel in to_save:
        src = factory_dir / rel
        if not src.exists():
            continue
        out = dest / rel
        out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        shutil.copy2(src, out)

    return dest if dest.exists() else None


# ── Init delegation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────


def _run_init(source: Path, target: Path) -> int:
    """Invoke the *sourced* init-factory to re-apply the install after the
    factory/ refresh. Subprocess so the replace-and-reinstall boundary and the
    sourced script's own idempotency/collision handling stay exactly the
    script's — update-factory adds no re-implementation of init's wiring."""
    pkg_init = source / "packages" / "factory" / "scripts" / "init-factory"
    init = pkg_init if pkg_init.exists() else source / "factory" / "scripts" / "init-factory"
    result = subprocess.run(
        [
            sys.executable,
            str(init),
            "--source",
            str(source),
            "--target",
            str(target),
        ],
        check=False,
    )
    return result.returncode


# ── Approval and preview ────────────────────────────────────────────────


def _show_update_preview(
    installed_version: str,
    candidate_version: str,
    source_label: str,
    source_selector: str,
    header_changes: dict,
    digest: str | None = None,
) -> None:
    """Display source, current/candidate versions, and planned effects
    before any download or mutation (ADR-0023 step 2)."""
    print("\nUpdate Preview")
    print("-" * 40)
    print(f"  Installed version:  {installed_version}")
    print(f"  Candidate version:  {candidate_version}")
    print(f"  Source:             {source_label} ({source_selector})")
    if digest:
        print(f"  Digest:             {digest}")
    print("\n  Planned effects:")
    print("    M  .agent-factory/factory/")
    for p in header_changes.get("added", []):
        print(f"    A  {p}")
    for p in header_changes.get("changed", []):
        print(f"    M  {p}")
    for p in header_changes.get("removed", []):
        print(f"    D  {p}  (no longer tracked)")
    print()


def get_update_consent(input_func=None) -> bool:
    """Ask for update consent. Blank, declined, or cancelled input is
    never treated as consent (VFO-023 approval gate)."""
    if input_func is None:
        input_func = input
    try:
        answer = input_func("Proceed with update? (yes to confirm): ")
    except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):
        return False
    return answer.strip().lower() in ("yes", "y")


# ── Source-boundary consent (ST-0286) ────────────────────────────────────


def _detect_source_boundary_change(
    manifest: dict, from_remote: str | None, from_local: Path | None,
) -> tuple[bool, str, str] | None:
    """Compare a requested --from-remote/--from-local source against the
    manifest's recorded source_selector/resolved_source or factory_source.

    Returns None when neither flag was given — no source change was
    requested, nothing to detect. Otherwise (changed, current_desc,
    requested_desc): `changed` is True only when the source kind differs
    (local<->remote) or, for two remote sources, the base URL differs
    (VFO-005). A different local path under the same "local" kind is not a
    boundary change — that is the pre-existing --source override, already
    in scope without separate consent.
    """
    if from_remote is None and from_local is None:
        return None

    current_kind = manifest.get("source_selector", "local")
    if current_kind == "remote":
        resolved_source = manifest.get("resolved_source") or ""
        current_value = (
            _derive_remote_base_url(resolved_source) or resolved_source or "unknown"
        )
    else:
        current_value = manifest.get("factory_source") or "unknown"
    current_desc = f"{current_kind} `{current_value}`"

    if from_remote is not None:
        requested_kind = "remote"
        requested_value = from_remote.rstrip("/")
    else:
        requested_kind = "local"
        requested_value = str(from_local.resolve())
    requested_desc = f"{requested_kind} `{requested_value}`"

    if requested_kind != current_kind:
        changed = True
    elif requested_kind == "remote":
        changed = current_value.rstrip("/") != requested_value
    else:
        changed = False

    return changed, current_desc, requested_desc


def _source_boundary_message(current_desc: str, requested_desc: str) -> str:
    return f"Current source: {current_desc}. Requested source: {requested_desc}."


def get_source_boundary_consent(message: str, input_func=None) -> bool:
    """Ask separate affirmative consent for a source-boundary change
    (VFO-005). Blank, declined, or cancelled input is never treated as
    consent, and this gate is never bypassed by --force — no automatic
    fallback crosses the source boundary."""
    if input_func is None:
        input_func = input
    print("\nSource-Boundary Change")
    print("-" * 40)
    print(f"  {message}")
    try:
        answer = input_func("Proceed with source change? (yes to confirm): ")
    except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):
        return False
    return answer.strip().lower() in ("yes", "y")


# ── Download, verification, and extraction (remote candidates) ──────────


def _download_and_verify_archive(
    resolved_base_url: str, timeout: int = REMOTE_TIMEOUT,
) -> tuple[str | None, bytes | None, str | None]:
    """Download SHA256SUMS and agent-factory.tar.gz, verify the digest.

    VFO-022: the archive is not extracted until its SHA-256 digest matches
    SHA256SUMS from the resolved release. A missing or mismatched digest
    returns an error and no bytes — no changes are made to the
    installation. Returns (error, archive_bytes, digest).
    """
    sums_url = resolved_base_url + "SHA256SUMS"
    error, sums_body = _fetch_url(sums_url, timeout=timeout)
    if error:
        return error, None, None

    archive_url = resolved_base_url + "agent-factory.tar.gz"
    error, archive_bytes = _fetch_url(archive_url, timeout=timeout)
    if error:
        return error, None, None

    expected_digest = None
    for line in sums_body.decode("utf-8", errors="replace").splitlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if not line:
            continue
        parts = line.split(None, 1)
        if len(parts) == 2 and parts[1].lstrip("*").strip() == "agent-factory.tar.gz":
            expected_digest = parts[0].strip()
            break

    actual_digest = hashlib.sha256(archive_bytes).hexdigest()

    if expected_digest is None:
        return (f"update-factory: no digest for agent-factory.tar.gz in "
                f"{sums_url}; refusing to extract"), None, None

    if expected_digest != actual_digest:
        return (f"update-factory: digest mismatch for agent-factory.tar.gz "
                f"(expected {expected_digest}, got {actual_digest}); "
                f"refusing to extract"), None, None

    return None, archive_bytes, actual_digest


def _safe_extract_archive(archive_bytes: bytes, dest: Path) -> None:
    """Extract a verified tar.gz's members into dest, refusing any path
    that would resolve outside dest (path-traversal guard)."""
    dest_resolved = dest.resolve()
    with tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(archive_bytes), mode="r:gz") as tf:
        for member in tf.getmembers():
            member_path = (dest / member.name).resolve()
            if member_path != dest_resolved and not str(member_path).startswith(
                    str(dest_resolved) + os.sep):
                raise ValueError(f"unsafe path in archive: {member.name}")
        tf.extractall(dest)


# ── Staging and application (ADR-0023 steps 4-6) ─────────────────────────


def _stage_factory_tree(target: Path, source_factory: Path) -> Path:
    """Copy the verified candidate factory/ tree into a staging directory
    alongside the current installation. The current installation is not
    touched — staging never modifies .agent-factory/factory/."""
    staging_dir = target / ".agent-factory" / f"{STAGING_DIR_PREFIX}{uuid.uuid4()}"
    shutil.copytree(source_factory, staging_dir)
    return staging_dir


def _apply_header_changes(
    target: Path, manifest: dict, header_changes: dict, candidate_source: Path,
) -> tuple[list[str], dict[str, bytes]]:
    """Apply planned instruction-header additions and content updates.

    Returns (changed_paths, backups) where backups maps each touched
    relative path to its original bytes, so a failed application can
    restore instruction headers exactly (VFO-023).
    """
    changed_paths: list[str] = []
    backups: dict[str, bytes] = {}
    cli_raw = manifest.get("cli")
    cli_name = cli_raw[0] if isinstance(cli_raw, list) and cli_raw else cli_raw
    if cli_name is None:
        return changed_paths, backups
    orientation = manifest.setdefault("orientation", {})

    for rel in header_changes.get("changed", []):
        fpath = target / rel
        if not fpath.is_file():
            continue
        new_block = _candidate_orientation_block(candidate_source, cli_name)
        if new_block is None:
            continue
        original = fpath.read_bytes()
        content = original.decode("utf-8")
        if ORIENTATION_BEGIN not in content or ORIENTATION_END not in content:
            continue
        start = content.index(ORIENTATION_BEGIN)
        end = content.index(ORIENTATION_END) + len(ORIENTATION_END)
        updated = content[:start] + new_block.rstrip("\n") + content[end:]
        backups[rel] = original
        fpath.write_text(updated, encoding="utf-8")
        digest = hashlib.sha256(new_block.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
        entry = orientation.get(rel)
        if isinstance(entry, dict):
            entry["block_digest"] = digest
        else:
            orientation[rel] = {"status": "injected", "block_digest": digest}
        changed_paths.append(rel)

    for rel in header_changes.get("added", []):
        fpath = target / rel
        if not fpath.is_file():
            continue
        original = fpath.read_bytes()
        content = original.decode("utf-8")
        if ORIENTATION_BEGIN in content:
            continue
        new_block = _candidate_orientation_block(candidate_source, cli_name)
        if new_block is None:
            continue
        orig_final_newline = content.endswith("\n") if content else True
        updated = new_block + "\n" + content
        backups[rel] = original
        fpath.write_text(updated, encoding="utf-8")
        digest = hashlib.sha256(new_block.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
        orientation[rel] = {
            "status": "injected",
            "block_digest": digest,
            "orig_final_newline": orig_final_newline,
        }
        changed_paths.append(rel)

    for rel in header_changes.get("removed", []):
        orientation.pop(rel, None)

    return changed_paths, backups


def _rollback_update(
    target: Path,
    target_factory: Path,
    backup_factory: Path | None,
    manifest_backup: bytes | None,
    checksums_backup: bytes | None,
    header_backups: dict[str, bytes],
) -> None:
    """Restore the previous Factory tree, manifest, checksums, and
    instruction headers after a failed application (ADR-0023 step 6)."""
    if target_factory.exists():
        if target_factory.is_dir():
            shutil.rmtree(target_factory)
        else:
            target_factory.unlink()
    if backup_factory is not None and backup_factory.is_dir():
        os.rename(backup_factory, target_factory)

    manifest_path = target / MANIFEST_PATH
    if manifest_backup is not None:
        manifest_path.write_bytes(manifest_backup)

    checksums_path = target / CHECKSUMS_PATH
    if checksums_backup is not None:
        checksums_path.write_bytes(checksums_backup)
    elif checksums_path.exists():
        checksums_path.unlink()

    for rel, original in header_backups.items():
        (target / rel).write_bytes(original)

    log("rolled back to the previous installation after a failed update")


def _write_manifest(target: Path, manifest: dict) -> None:
    manifest_path = target / MANIFEST_PATH
    manifest_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    manifest_path.write_text(
        json.dumps(manifest, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8",
    )


def _show_receipt(
    source_label: str,
    source_selector: str,
    resolved_version: str,
    digest: str | None,
    changed_paths: list[str],
    preserved_path: str | None = None,
    preserved_files: list[str] | None = None,
) -> None:
    """Display the update receipt (ADR-0023 step 7 / VFO-025)."""
    print("\nUpdate Receipt")
    print("-" * 40)
    print(f"  Source:             {source_label} ({source_selector})")
    print(f"  Resolved version:   {resolved_version}")
    if digest:
        print(f"  Digest:             {digest}")
    print("\n  Changed paths:")
    for p in sorted(set(changed_paths)):
        print(f"    {p}")
    if preserved_files:
        print(f"\n  Preserved user changes ({preserved_path}):")
        for p in preserved_files:
            print(f"    {p}")
    print()


# ── Check mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


def _read_candidate_version_local(source: Path) -> str:
    """Read the Factory version from a local candidate source tree."""
    version_file = source / "packages" / "factory" / "VERSION"
    if version_file.is_file():
        return version_file.read_text().strip()
    return "unknown"


def _fetch_url(url: str, timeout: int = REMOTE_TIMEOUT, method: str = "GET"):
    """Fetch a URL. Returns (error, body_bytes)."""
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, method=method)
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:
            return None, resp.read()
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        return f"failed to fetch {url}: HTTP {e.code} {e.reason}", None
    except urllib.error.URLError as e:
        return f"failed to fetch {url}: {e.reason}", None
    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:
        return f"failed to fetch {url}: {e}", None


class _NoFollowRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
    """Suppress automatic redirect following so the 3xx response's Location
    header can be read directly, matching install-agent-factory's release
    resolution (ST-0282) without requiring the redirect target itself to be
    independently fetchable."""

    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):
        return None


def _resolve_release_base_url(base_url: str, timeout: int = REMOTE_TIMEOUT):
    """Resolve `<base_url>/latest`'s redirect to an immutable release URL.

    Same resolution `install-agent-factory` uses for a version-less remote
    install (ST-0282): a HEAD request to `<base>/latest` whose 3xx Location
    header names the current release. Returns (error, resolved_url) where
    resolved_url ends with '/'.
    """
    base = base_url.rstrip("/")
    latest_url = f"{base}/latest"
    opener = urllib.request.build_opener(_NoFollowRedirect)
    req = urllib.request.Request(latest_url, method="HEAD")
    try:
        with opener.open(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:
            return f"{latest_url} did not redirect to a release (HTTP {resp.status})", None
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        if e.code in (301, 302, 303, 307, 308):
            location = e.headers.get("Location")
            if not location:
                return f"redirect from {latest_url} had no Location header", None
            resolved = urllib.parse.urljoin(latest_url, location)
            if not resolved.endswith("/"):
                resolved += "/"
            return None, resolved
        return f"failed to fetch {latest_url}: HTTP {e.code} {e.reason}", None
    except urllib.error.URLError as e:
        return f"failed to fetch {latest_url}: {e.reason}", None
    except (TimeoutError, OSError) as e:
        return f"failed to fetch {latest_url}: {e}", None


def _fetch_candidate_digest(resolved_url: str, timeout: int = REMOTE_TIMEOUT):
    """Read SHA256SUMS at a resolved release URL and return the digest for
    agent-factory.tar.gz, without downloading the archive itself — --check
    reports the candidate digest but must not write, and downloading the
    full archive just to hash it is unnecessary for a report.

    Returns (error, digest).
    """
    error, body = _fetch_url(resolved_url + "SHA256SUMS", timeout=timeout)
    if error:
        return error, None
    for line in body.decode("utf-8", errors="replace").splitlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if not line:
            continue
        parts = line.split(None, 1)
        if len(parts) == 2 and parts[1].lstrip("*").strip() == "agent-factory.tar.gz":
            return None, parts[0].strip()
    return f"no digest for agent-factory.tar.gz in {resolved_url}SHA256SUMS", None


def _derive_remote_base_url(resolved_source: str) -> str | None:
    """Recover the release base URL from a previously resolved release URL.

    The manifest records only the immutable, version-pinned release URL
    (e.g. `https://host/releases/1.0.0/`) — the mutable base URL used to
    check for a newer release is not stored separately. Strip the
    `/releases/<version>/` suffix to recover it. Returns None if
    resolved_source does not match that shape.
    """
    if not resolved_source:
        return None
    idx = resolved_source.find("/releases/")
    if idx == -1:
        return None
    return resolved_source[:idx]


def _resolve_remote_candidate(resolved_source: str, timeout: int = REMOTE_TIMEOUT):
    """Resolve the candidate version and digest for a remote-sourced install.

    Returns (error, candidate_version, resolved_url, digest). On error,
    candidate_version and/or digest may still be None; the caller reports
    what it has.
    """
    base_url = _derive_remote_base_url(resolved_source)
    if base_url is None:
        return (f"cannot determine the release base URL from the recorded "
                f"source {resolved_source!r}"), None, None, None

    return _resolve_remote_candidate_from_base(base_url, timeout=timeout)


def _resolve_remote_candidate_from_base(base_url: str, timeout: int = REMOTE_TIMEOUT):
    """Resolve the candidate version, release URL, and digest starting from
    an explicit remote base URL, rather than one derived from a previously
    resolved release URL. Used for --from-remote (ST-0286), where the base
    URL is given directly and may name a different remote host entirely.

    Returns (error, candidate_version, resolved_url, digest), same shape as
    `_resolve_remote_candidate`.
    """
    error, resolved_url = _resolve_release_base_url(base_url, timeout=timeout)
    if error:
        return error, None, None, None

    match = re.search(r"/releases/([^/]+)/?$", resolved_url)
    candidate_version = match.group(1) if match else "unknown"

    error, digest = _fetch_candidate_digest(resolved_url, timeout=timeout)
    if error:
        return error, candidate_version, resolved_url, None

    return None, candidate_version, resolved_url, digest


def _discover_instruction_files(target: Path) -> list[str]:
    """Relative paths of AGENTS.md / copilot-instructions.md under target,
    mirroring install-agent-factory's discovery rule."""
    found = []
    for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(target, followlinks=False):
        dirnames[:] = [d for d in dirnames if d not in INSTRUCTION_SCAN_SKIP_DIRS]
        for fname in filenames:
            if fname in INSTRUCTION_FILENAMES:
                fpath = Path(dirpath) / fname
                if fpath.is_file():
                    found.append(fpath.relative_to(target).as_posix())
    return sorted(found)


def _candidate_orientation_block(source: Path, cli_name: str) -> str | None:
    """Build the orientation block text a *local* candidate source would
    inject for cli_name, for digest comparison against the installed
    block_digest. Returns None when the CLI's config source is unavailable
    in `source` — comparison is then skipped rather than guessed."""
    dot_dirs = CLI_DOT_DIRS.get(cli_name, [])
    dot_dir = dot_dirs[0] if dot_dirs else ""

    if dot_dir in ORIENTATION_INCLUDE:
        content = ORIENTATION_INCLUDE[dot_dir]
    else:
        cli_file = CLI_ORIENTATION_FILE.get(dot_dir, "")
        if not cli_file:
            return None
        config_path = source / "packages" / "factory" / "config" / cli_file
        if not config_path.is_file():
            return None
        content = config_path.read_text()

    return f"{ORIENTATION_BEGIN}\n{content}{ORIENTATION_END}\n"


def _injected_orientation_paths(orientation: dict) -> set[str]:
    """Paths whose orientation entry records an injected header block —
    the only entries --check's header-change report concerns itself with.
    Linked/external entries are symlink bookkeeping, not header content."""
    paths = set()
    for path, entry in orientation.items():
        status = entry.get("status") if isinstance(entry, dict) else entry
        if status == "injected":
            paths.add(path)
    return paths


def _detect_header_changes(target: Path, manifest: dict, source: Path | None) -> dict:
    """Compare installed instruction headers (manifest orientation entries)
    against the current target tree and, when a local candidate source is
    available, against what that candidate would produce.

    Returns {"added": [...], "removed": [...], "changed": [...]}. `added`
    and `removed` need only the target tree. `changed` (content differs
    from what the candidate would produce) is populated only when `source`
    is given — a remote candidate would require downloading the archive to
    compare content, which --check must not do.
    """
    orientation = manifest.get("orientation") or {}
    known = _injected_orientation_paths(orientation)
    current = set(_discover_instruction_files(target))

    added = sorted(current - known)
    removed = sorted(known - current)
    changed = []

    cli_raw = manifest.get("cli")
    cli_name = cli_raw[0] if isinstance(cli_raw, list) and cli_raw else cli_raw
    if source is not None and cli_name:
        candidate_block = _candidate_orientation_block(source, cli_name)
        if candidate_block is not None:
            candidate_digest = hashlib.sha256(
                candidate_block.encode("utf-8")
            ).hexdigest()
            for path in sorted(known & current):
                entry = orientation.get(path)
                stored_digest = (
                    entry.get("block_digest") if isinstance(entry, dict) else None
                )
                if stored_digest and stored_digest != candidate_digest:
                    changed.append(path)

    return {"added": added, "removed": removed, "changed": changed}


def _run_check(target: Path, manifest: dict, args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    """Report installed/candidate versions, source, digest, local
    modifications, and planned header changes. Never writes — no files,
    directories, staging areas, or manifest updates (VFO-021)."""
    print("\nUpdate Check")
    print("-" * 40)

    installed_version = manifest.get("factory_version", "unknown")
    source_selector = manifest.get("source_selector", "local")
    resolved_source = manifest.get("resolved_source")

    candidate_version = "unknown"
    candidate_digest = None
    candidate_error: str | None = None
    local_source: Path | None = None
    source_label = resolved_source or manifest.get("factory_source") or "unknown"

    if args.source is not None:
        local_source = args.source.resolve()
        candidate_version = _read_candidate_version_local(local_source)
        source_label = str(local_source)
    elif source_selector == "remote":
        if not resolved_source:
            candidate_error = "no resolved_source recorded for this remote install"
        else:
            candidate_error, candidate_version, resolved_url, candidate_digest = \
                _resolve_remote_candidate(resolved_source)
            candidate_version = candidate_version or "unknown"
            if resolved_url:
                source_label = resolved_url
    else:
        factory_source = manifest.get("factory_source")
        if not factory_source:
            candidate_error = "no factory_source recorded — pass --source"
        else:
            local_source = Path(factory_source)
            if not local_source.is_dir():
                candidate_error = f"recorded source not found: {local_source}"
            else:
                candidate_version = _read_candidate_version_local(local_source)
                source_label = str(local_source)

    print(f"  Installed version:  {installed_version}")
    if candidate_error:
        print(f"  Candidate version:  unavailable ({candidate_error})")
    else:
        print(f"  Candidate version:  {candidate_version}")
        if installed_version != "unknown" and installed_version == candidate_version:
            print("  (installed and candidate versions are equal)")
    print(f"  Source:             {source_label} ({source_selector})")
    if candidate_digest:
        print(f"  Candidate digest:   {candidate_digest}")

    result = _detect_modifications(target)
    if result is None:
        print("\n  No checksum baseline found (pre-checksum install) — "
              "cannot detect modifications.")
    else:
        modified, added, removed = result
        if modified or added or removed:
            _report_modifications(modified, added, removed)
        else:
            print("\n  No local modifications detected.")

    headers = _detect_header_changes(target, manifest, local_source)
    if headers["added"] or headers["removed"] or headers["changed"]:
        print("\n  Planned instruction header changes:")
        for p in headers["added"]:
            print(f"    A  {p}")
        for p in headers["removed"]:
            print(f"    D  {p}")
        for p in headers["changed"]:
            print(f"    M  {p}")
    else:
        print("\n  No planned instruction header changes.")

    source_boundary = _detect_source_boundary_change(
        manifest, args.from_remote, args.from_local,
    )
    if source_boundary is not None:
        changed, current_desc, requested_desc = source_boundary
        if changed:
            print(
                f"\n  Source change detected: current {current_desc}, "
                f"requested {requested_desc}. This update would require "
                "separate source-boundary consent."
            )

    print()
    return 0


# ── Main ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    ap.add_argument("--target", type=Path, default=Path("."))
    ap.add_argument(
        "--source",
        type=Path,
        default=None,
        help="agent_factory checkout whose factory/ is the new state "
        "(default: the source recorded in the install manifest)",
    )
    ap.add_argument(
        "--force",
        action="store_true",
        help="proceed even when user modifications are detected; "
        "changed files are preserved under .agent-factory/factory-user-changes/",
    )
    ap.add_argument(
        "--check",
        action="store_true",
        help="report user modifications and exit without updating",
    )
    source_boundary_group = ap.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    source_boundary_group.add_argument(
        "--from-remote",
        type=str,
        default=None,
        metavar="URL",
        help="update from a different remote base URL; a source kind or "
        "URL change requires separate consent (ST-0286)",
    )
    source_boundary_group.add_argument(
        "--from-local",
        type=Path,
        default=None,
        metavar="PATH",
        help="update from a local checkout; a source kind change requires "
        "separate consent (ST-0286)",
    )
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)

    target = args.target.resolve()
    try:
        manifest = load_manifest(target)
    except ManifestUnreadable as exc:
        print(
            f"update-factory: {CHECKSUMS_PATH} exists but is not valid JSON ({exc})",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return 1
    if manifest is None:
        print(
            f"update-factory: {target} is not an init-factory'd project — "
            f"no {MANIFEST_PATH} found",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return 1

    if args.check:
        return _run_check(target, manifest, args)

    # ── Source-boundary consent (ST-0286) ────────────────────────────────
    # A separate gate from the normal update approval below, and never
    # bypassed by --force (VFO-005). No automatic fallback crosses the
    # source boundary — only an explicit "yes" here lets the update
    # proceed with the requested source; blank/declined input stops with
    # no changes at all, before modification detection even runs.

    source_boundary = _detect_source_boundary_change(
        manifest, args.from_remote, args.from_local,
    )
    if source_boundary is not None:
        changed, current_desc, requested_desc = source_boundary
        if changed:
            message = _source_boundary_message(current_desc, requested_desc)
            if not get_source_boundary_consent(message):
                print(
                    "update-factory: source change cancelled — no changes made",
                    file=sys.stderr,
                )
                return 1

    # ── Modification detection ─────────────────────────────────────────
    # Runs before staging or approval: a modified installation stops the
    # update before the user is even asked to approve one (VFO-024).

    preserved_path: str | None = None
    preserved_files: list[str] | None = None

    result = _detect_modifications(target)
    if result is not None:
        modified, added, removed = result
        has_changes = bool(modified or added or removed)

        if has_changes:
            _report_modifications(modified, added, removed)

            if not args.force:
                print(
                    "  User modifications detected. The update would replace these.\n"
                    "  Options:\n"
                    "    --force   proceed and preserve changed files in\n"
                    f"              {USER_CHANGES_DIR}/<timestamp>/\n"
                    "    --check   re-run with --check to see the full report\n",
                    file=sys.stderr,
                )
                return 2

            saved = _preserve_user_changes(target, modified, added)
            if saved:
                preserved_path = str(saved)
                preserved_files = modified + added
                log(f"preserved {len(preserved_files)} user-changed files in {saved}")
    else:
        log("no checksum baseline — proceeding (first update will record baseline)")

    installed_version = manifest.get("factory_version", "unknown")
    source_selector = manifest.get("source_selector", "local")
    if args.from_remote is not None:
        source_selector = "remote"
    elif args.from_local is not None:
        source_selector = "local"

    # --from-local behaves like --source for the local-candidate branch
    # below; --from-remote is handled separately since it names a base URL,
    # not a resolved release URL already recorded in the manifest.
    local_source_arg = args.from_local if args.from_local is not None else args.source
    is_remote = source_selector == "remote" and local_source_arg is None

    target_factory = target / ".agent-factory" / "factory"
    if target_factory.exists() and not target_factory.is_dir():
        print(
            f"update-factory: {target_factory} exists and is not a directory — "
            "refusing to touch it",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return 1

    # ── Resolve candidate (read-only; no download of the archive yet) ───

    resolved_url: str | None = None
    digest: str | None = None
    source: Path | None = None
    source_factory: Path | None = None

    if is_remote:
        if args.from_remote is not None:
            error, candidate_version, resolved_url, digest = \
                _resolve_remote_candidate_from_base(args.from_remote)
        else:
            resolved_source = manifest.get("resolved_source")
            if not resolved_source:
                print(
                    "update-factory: no resolved_source recorded for this "
                    "remote install",
                    file=sys.stderr,
                )
                return 1
            error, candidate_version, resolved_url, digest = \
                _resolve_remote_candidate(resolved_source)
        if error:
            print(f"update-factory: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        source_label = resolved_url
        preview_candidate_source = None
    else:
        if local_source_arg is not None:
            source = local_source_arg.resolve()
        else:
            recorded = manifest.get("factory_source")
            if not isinstance(recorded, str) or not recorded:
                print(
                    "update-factory: no --source given and the install manifest "
                    "records no factory_source (a pre-existing install?) — pass "
                    "--source <agent_factory checkout>",
                    file=sys.stderr,
                )
                return 1
            source = Path(recorded).resolve()

        pkg_factory = source / "packages" / "factory"
        source_factory = pkg_factory if pkg_factory.is_dir() else source / ".agent-factory" / "factory"
        if not source_factory.is_dir():
            print(
                f"update-factory: no packages/factory/ found at {source} — pass "
                "--source explicitly",
                file=sys.stderr,
            )
            return 1

        candidate_version = _read_candidate_version_local(source)
        source_label = str(source)
        preview_candidate_source = source

    header_changes = _detect_header_changes(target, manifest, preview_candidate_source)

    # ── Approval (ADR-0023 step 2) — before download or mutation ────────

    _show_update_preview(
        installed_version, candidate_version, source_label, source_selector,
        header_changes, digest,
    )
    if not get_update_consent():
        print("update-factory: update cancelled — no changes made", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    # ── Download and verification (remote candidates only) ──────────────
    # VFO-022: verified before any extraction or mutation.

    scratch_root: Path | None = None
    if is_remote:
        error, archive_bytes, digest = _download_and_verify_archive(resolved_url)
        if error:
            print(f"update-factory: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        scratch_root = target / ".agent-factory" / f"{REMOTE_SCRATCH_PREFIX}{uuid.uuid4()}"
        factory_dir = scratch_root / "packages" / "factory"
        factory_dir.mkdir(parents=True)
        try:
            _safe_extract_archive(archive_bytes, factory_dir)
        except Exception as exc:
            shutil.rmtree(scratch_root, ignore_errors=True)
            print(f"update-factory: failed to extract archive: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        source = scratch_root
        source_factory = factory_dir

    # Recompute header changes now that verified candidate content is on
    # disk — the preview above could only report added/removed for a
    # remote candidate, never content changes (that would need the
    # archive downloaded, which approval must precede).
    header_changes = _detect_header_changes(target, manifest, source)

    # ── Staging (ADR-0023 step 4) ────────────────────────────────────────
    # The verified replacement is staged alongside the current
    # installation. Nothing under .agent-factory/factory/ is touched yet.

    staging_dir = _stage_factory_tree(target, source_factory)
    log(f"staged verified replacement at {staging_dir}")

    # ── Application (ADR-0023 step 5), with rollback on failure (step 6) ─

    manifest_path = target / MANIFEST_PATH
    checksums_path = target / CHECKSUMS_PATH
    manifest_backup = manifest_path.read_bytes() if manifest_path.is_file() else None
    checksums_backup = checksums_path.read_bytes() if checksums_path.is_file() else None

    backup: Path | None = None
    if target_factory.is_dir():
        _unlock_factory(target_factory)
        backup = target / ".agent-factory" / f"{BACKUP_DIR_PREFIX}{uuid.uuid4()}"
        os.rename(target_factory, backup)
        log(f"moved existing .agent-factory/factory/ aside ({target_factory})")
    os.rename(staging_dir, target_factory)

    changed_header_paths: list[str] = []
    header_backups: dict[str, bytes] = {}
    apply_error: str | None = None
    code = 0
    try:
        changed_header_paths, header_backups = _apply_header_changes(
            target, manifest, header_changes, source,
        )
        code = _run_init(source, target)
        if code != 0:
            apply_error = "the sourced init-factory did not complete"
    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 — any apply failure rolls back
        apply_error = str(exc)
        code = code or 1

    if apply_error is not None:
        _rollback_update(
            target, target_factory, backup, manifest_backup, checksums_backup,
            header_backups,
        )
        if scratch_root is not None:
            shutil.rmtree(scratch_root, ignore_errors=True)
        print(
            f"update-factory: {apply_error} — see output above; the "
            "previous installation has been restored",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return code if code else 1

    if backup is not None and backup.is_dir():
        shutil.rmtree(backup)
        log("removed the update backup")

    # Purge stale bytecode so a prior Python version's .pyc never shadows
    # the freshly installed source.
    for pycache in sorted(target_factory.rglob("__pycache__")):
        shutil.rmtree(pycache)
    log("purged stale __pycache__ directories")

    # ── Receipt (ADR-0023 step 7 / VFO-025) ──────────────────────────────

    manifest["factory_version"] = candidate_version
    manifest["source_selector"] = source_selector
    if is_remote:
        manifest["resolved_source"] = resolved_url
        manifest["archive_sha256"] = digest or ""
    else:
        manifest["factory_source"] = str(source)
    _write_manifest(target, manifest)

    _stamp_tree_hash(source, target)
    _write_checksums(target, target_factory)
    _lock_factory(target_factory)

    if scratch_root is not None:
        shutil.rmtree(scratch_root, ignore_errors=True)

    changed_paths = [".agent-factory/factory/"] + changed_header_paths
    _show_receipt(
        source_label, source_selector, candidate_version, digest,
        changed_paths, preserved_path, preserved_files,
    )

    log("done, .agent-factory/factory/ is now current")
    return 0


def _stamp_tree_hash(source: Path, target: Path) -> None:
    """Record the git tree hash of packages/factory/ in the install manifest
    so check-factory-freshness can detect staleness without a full diff."""
    pkg_factory = source / "packages" / "factory"
    if not pkg_factory.is_dir():
        return
    try:
        tree_hash = subprocess.run(
            ["git", "-C", str(source), "rev-parse", "HEAD:packages/factory"],
            capture_output=True, text=True, check=True,
        ).stdout.strip()
    except (subprocess.CalledProcessError, FileNotFoundError):
        return
    manifest_path = target / MANIFEST_PATH
    if not manifest_path.is_file():
        return
    try:
        manifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):
        return
    manifest["factory_tree_hash"] = tree_hash
    manifest_path.write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    log(f"stamped factory_tree_hash: {tree_hash[:12]}")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
